113	        return this.telephone;
114	    }
116	    public void setTelephone(String telephone) {
117	        this.telephone = telephone;
118	    }
```
(Also referenced in `toString()` at line 286.)

### Normalizer: `OwnerTelephone`
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerTelephone.java` — a `final` utility with a private constructor and a single static method `public static String toE164(String input) throws InvalidTelephoneException`. It strips spaces/dashes/brackets, keeps a leading `+`/country code or assumes `+61` (dropping a leading `0`), enforces 8–15 digits, and enforces exact national-number lengths for `+61` (9) and `+1` (10). Example: `"0412 345 678"` → `"+61412345678"`. This is the project's own phone formatting utility (see item 5 — there is no libphonenumber).

### Exception + handler
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/InvalidTelephoneException.java`
```java
public class InvalidTelephoneException extends Exception {
    public InvalidTelephoneException(String telephone) {
        super("Telephone cannot be normalized to a valid E.164 number: " + telephone);
    }
}
```
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler.java`
```java
public void handle(@Parameter InvalidTelephoneException ex,
        ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<Map<String, List<String>>>> response) {
    response.send(ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST)
            .body(Map.of("errors", List.of("telephone"))));   // responds 400
}
```

### Identity utility: `OwnerIdentities`
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/OwnerIdentities.java` — builds the owner identity key/customer code using `normalizeTelephone(owner.getTelephone())`, which delegates to `OwnerTelephone.toE164(...)` and falls back to the raw value on `InvalidTelephoneException` (lines 31, 46, 86–93).

### Other owner-function files referencing telephone
`ValidateOwner.java`, `ValidateOwnerFields.java`, `ApplyOwner.java`, `AssignCustomerCode.java`, `CheckPossibleDuplicate.java` (all under `.../rest/function/owner/`).

### JDBC repositories (SQL column mapping)
`.../repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, `JdbcPetRepositoryImpl.java`, `JdbcVisitRepositoryImpl.java`.

Note: there is no `OwnerResponse` class. Response DTOs are the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` (package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`), generated at build time into `target/generated-sources` from the spec (see items 2 and 4). Pets/vets have no telephone field — only owners do.

## 2. `from(...)` factory methods building a response DTO from an entity

None exist. There is no `static ... from(...)` factory anywhere under `src/main/java`, and no `OwnerResponse.from`. Instead, entity→DTO conversion is done by a MapStruct mapper:

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`
```java
@Mapper(uses = PetMapper.class)
public interface OwnerMapper {
    @Mapping(target = "displayName",
            expression = "java(owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName())")
    @Mapping(target = "initials", expression = "java(...)")
    @Mapping(target = "membershipLevel", expression = "java(...MembershipLevels.levelFor(owner))")
    @Mapping(target = "locality", expression = "java(...Localities.localityFor(owner))")
    @Mapping(target = "contactPreference", expression = "java(...ContactPreferences.preferenceFor(owner))")
    @Mapping(target = "ageBand", expression = "java(...AgeBands.bandFor(owner))")
    @Mapping(target = "identityKey", expression = "java(...OwnerIdentities.identityKey(owner))")
    @Mapping(target = "checkDigit", expression = "java(...CheckDigits.checkDigitFor(owner))")
    OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);
    ...
}
```
`toOwnerDto(Owner)` is the effective "build a response DTO from an entity" method. Note it does NOT currently map any `telephoneDisplay` target. The response is emitted in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RespondWithOwner.java` via `response.send(ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner))`.

## 3. Tests referencing "telephone"/"telephoneDisplay"

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` (the ONLY reference to `telephoneDisplay` in the whole repo):
```java
7	/** telephone-display: 'telephoneDisplay' is the stored E.164 number formatted for humans
8	 * (country code, space, national digits grouped in threes); raw 'telephone' stays E.164. A fixed
9	 * input gives an exact expected display. */
